TABLE 1: SHAREPOINT & DATA GOVERNANCE STRATEGIC ROADMAP
================================================================================

1. Feature / Product: "Reimagined" Architecture
Target Date: Late 2025 - 2026
Pros: Faster site creation; natively integrates AI; modern, cohesive user experience.
Cons: Steep learning curve for current site owners; heavily customized legacy sites may break.
Implementation Considerations: Conduct a full audit of classic/customized sites before rollout. Require mandatory change management training for intranet creators.
Source URL: https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?id=547732

2. Feature / Product: Restricted Access Control (RAC)
Target Date: Available Now
Pros: Prevents AI oversharing; enforces strict Zero Trust boundaries at the site level via Entra ID.
Cons: High admin overhead; poor Entra ID group hygiene will instantly block valid users.
Implementation Considerations: Clean up Entra ID security groups first. Test RAC in "audit mode" on a single department before global enforcement.
Source URL: https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/sharepoint/restricted-access-control

3. Feature / Product: AI-Assisted FAQ Web Parts
Target Date: May 2026
Pros: Drastically reduces manual content updates; keeps organizational knowledge fresh.
Cons: Risk of AI "hallucinations" suggesting incorrect or out-of-context updates.
Implementation Considerations: Establish strict governance: AI suggestions must always be reviewed and approved by a human site owner before publishing.
Source URL: https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?id=482198

4. Feature / Product: SharePoint Agents (Viva Engage)
Target Date: 2026
Pros: Deflects IT/HR helpdesk tickets by providing instant, grounded answers to employees.
Cons: If underlying SharePoint files are messy or outdated, the Agent will confidently give wrong answers.
Implementation Considerations: The "Data Clean-up" phase of your Year 1 roadmap is a non-negotiable prerequisite. Garbage data equals garbage Agent answers.
Source URL: https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?filters=SharePoint

5. Feature / Product: Bulk Data Lifecycle (Purview)
Target Date: December 2026
Pros: Massive time-saver for compliance teams managing retention at an enterprise scale.
Cons: A poorly written KQL query could accidentally delete or retain the wrong massive dataset.
Implementation Considerations: Restrict tool access to senior compliance admins only. Mandate that all KQL queries run in a simulation environment before execution.
Source URL: https://www.microsoft.com/en-us/microsoft-365/roadmap?id=392457


