TABLE 2: MICROSOFT 365 CORE STRATEGIC ROADMAP (COPILOT, AGENTS, LTSC)
================================================================================

1. Strategic Initiative: Agentic AI (Agent Mode)
Target Date: Early - Mid 2026
Pros: Massive productivity gains; automates complex, multi-step tasks natively on the canvas in Excel, Word, and PPT.
Cons: High licensing costs ($30/user/mo); severe user frustration if they lack prompt engineering skills.
Implementation Considerations: Shift training away from "how to click buttons" to "how to manage an AI assistant." Invest heavily in role-based prompt training.
Source URL: https://techcommunity.microsoft.com/blog/microsoftteamsblog/what%E2%80%99s-new-in-microsoft-teams--microsoft-ignite-2025/4470387

2. Strategic Initiative: Teams Facilitator Agent
Target Date: Mid-2025 to 2026
Pros: Eliminates manual note-taking; automatically pushes action items directly to Planner.
Cons: Privacy concerns regarding constant meeting transcription; nuance can be lost in AI summaries.
Implementation Considerations: Update corporate HR and meeting policies regarding AI transcription consent. Train users to actively review AI notes.
Source URL: https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?id=478611

3. Strategic Initiative: Microsoft Agent 365
Target Date: 2026
Pros: Centralized IT visibility; prevents unchecked "AI sprawl" across the organization.
Cons: Adds another complex admin center for your IT team to learn and manage.
Implementation Considerations: Align IT, Security, and Legal teams to define global AI guardrails before opening up custom Agent creation to standard business users.
Source URL: https://techcommunity.microsoft.com/blog/copilotadminupdates

4. Strategic Initiative: M365 Pricing Update
Target Date: July 1, 2026
Pros: Bundles premium tools (Intune Suite, Defender P1) into E3/E5, enabling major vendor consolidation.
Cons: Immediate budget shock, particularly the massive ~25% to 29% hike for Frontline (F3) workers.
Implementation Considerations: Act immediately. Audit F3 ghost accounts and aggressively cancel redundant 3rd-party tools (like Workspace ONE) before July.
Source URL: https://www.microsoft.com/en-us/licensing/news/2026-M365-Packaging-Pricing-Updates

5. Strategic Initiative: Zero Trust & Edge Security
Target Date: December 2026
Pros: Strong defense against data leaks; persistent watermarks deter screen-capturing sensitive data.
Cons: Can cause user friction or browser performance hits if policies are overly restrictive.
Implementation Considerations: Pilot watermarking with high-risk departments first (Finance/Execs). Communicate clearly why watermarks are appearing.
Source URL: https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/purview/purview

6. Strategic Initiative: Office 2024 LTSC End of Support
Target Date: October 9, 2029
Pros: Forces legacy technical debt clean-up; keeps air-gapped networks compliant and secure.
Cons: Highly manual, expensive deployment process for disconnected environments.
Implementation Considerations: Strictly define who actually needs to be offline. Budget and plan for the successor ("Office 2028 LTSC") in Year 3 to ensure testing runway.
Source URL: https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/lifecycle/products/office-ltsc-2024


